      "filename": "HMS Hood vs HMS Renown propeller nugget.jpg",
      "title": "File:HMS Hood vs HMS Renown propeller nugget.jpg",
      "url": "https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/0/02/HMS_Hood_vs_HMS_Renown_propeller_nugget.jpg",
      "descriptionUrl": "https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:HMS_Hood_vs_HMS_Renown_propeller_nugget.jpg",
      "width": 3888,
      "height": 2592,
      "mime": "image/jpeg",
      "license": "CC BY-SA 3.0",
      "licenseUrl": "http://creativecommons.org/licenses/by-sa/3.0/",
      "artist": "Ultrastarx1",
      "credit": "en:file:HMS_Hood_vs_HMS_Renown_propeller_nugget.jpg",
      "source": "HMS Hood vs HMS Renown propeller nugget",
      "description": "Hms Hood vs HMS Renown 1935 picture of propeller nugget\n\nAs a result of a collision off the coast of Spain on 23 January 1935, one of Hood's propellers struck the bow of Renown. While dry-docked for repairs, Renown had fragments of this propeller removed from her bilge section. The pieces of the propeller were kept by dockyard workers: \"Hood\" v \"Renown\" Jan. 23rd. 1935 was stamped on one surviving example, and \"Hood V Renown off Arosa 23–1–35\" on another. Of the known surviving pieces, one is privately held and another was given by the Hood family to the Hood Association in 2006. Relics and Artefacts from Hood Recently a third piece has come to light in Glasgow, where the Hood was built. It is held by a private collector and stamped HMS HOOD v HMS RENOWN 23 1 35. HMS Hood v HMS Renown propeller fragment",
      "dateCreated": "19 November 2007 (upload time)",
      "sourceType": "core",
      "sourceArticleId": "hms-hood-wp",
      "sourceGeohash4": "g732"
    },
